    "body": "## Summary\n- add a DB-backed per-account password-recovery cooldown (default 60s, constrained to 15-900s)\n- perform the cooldown check while holding the existing pessimistic user lock so concurrent requests cannot bypass it\n- preserve enumeration resistance: suppressed requests still return the same public 202 and keep the existing token valid\n- expose production configuration and document the abuse-control contract\n- add regression coverage ensuring a repeated request neither invalidates the current token nor queues another email\n\n## Launch priority\nP1 abuse protection / authentication boundary hardening. This is defense-in-depth and intentionally does not claim to replace edge/IP-aware rate limiting.\n\n## Validation expected\nCI: Maven verify, web tests/lint/build, production Compose contract, runtime smokes.",
